course: dictionary
lesson: 2932
title: Drawstring: a cord that tightens
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A drawstring is a cord threaded through the top of a bag, or through the waist or hood of clothes. When you pull its ends, the opening gets tighter. The words around it give you clues: «drawstring bag» and «pull the drawstring» tell you what it is for.
explain: Read the sentence, then ask: what would fit here? «Cords, drawstrings and scarves on clothes can catch on playground equipment» tells you a drawstring is a cord, and a cord can get caught. Swap in your meaning to check it still makes sense.
explain: Some words also carry a warning. «A boy in Wisconsin went down a slide with a drawstring hoodie on; the cord caught at the top» shows why long drawstrings can be dangerous for young children.
fact: A drawstring is a cord that tightens an opening when you pull it.
fact: «Drawstring bag» means a bag closed by pulling a cord threaded through its top.
fact: «Drawstring waist» means the waist of clothes can be tightened with a cord.
fact: Long drawstrings on hoods can catch on playground equipment or bus doors, so they should be short or removed for young children.
fact: A hedgehog's ring of muscle pulls its skin tight, a bit like the string on a drawstring bag.
exercise: What does a drawstring do when you pull it? | Makes the bag float | Changes the colour of the bag | *Makes the opening tighter | Makes the bag heavier
exercise: Which thing is a drawstring? | A zip that runs up the side | A button on a coat | A pocket on the front of a shirt | *A cord threaded through the top of a bag
exercise: «Cords, drawstrings and scarves on clothes can catch on playground equipment and pull tight around your neck.» Why should a young child's hood have short drawstrings? | So the hood is warmer | So the hood looks bigger | *So they do not catch on playground equipment and pull tight around the neck | So the hood can be worn as a hat
test: «When it is scared, a ring of muscle pulls its skin tight like the string on a drawstring bag.» What does the hedgehog's skin do? | Falls off in strips | Grows long and soft | *Pulls tight, like a bag closing | Turns bright red
test: What is the main job of a drawstring? | Keeps water out of a tent | Makes a sound like a bell | *Pulls an opening tighter | Holds a book open
exam: Ella finds the word drawstring in a safety leaflet. Which explanation fits best? | A kind of hedgehog | A bus door that opens slowly | *A cord you pull to make an opening tighter | A bag with a zip and two pockets
